    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">穴居的爬行類類人生物狗頭人，崇拜邪惡龍爲半神，並作爲其手下與諂媚者爲其服務。狗頭人會把握機會住進龍巢裏，但更多時候卻是成羣結隊的棲息在地下城中，四處收集寶藏和廉價首飾以豐富它們卑微的小寶庫。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>人丁興旺Strength in Numbers。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">狗頭人是卵生生物。它們迅速成熟且甚至可作爲“巨龍great wyrms”存活超過一世紀。然而，事實上很多狗頭人在十歲之前就會死去。身體孱弱的它們不過是掠食者的一碟小菜，由於易受攻擊而不得不團結一致。狗頭人壓倒性的數量往往可以在戰鬥中戰勝強大的對手，但這往往伴隨著狗頭人一方慘重的傷亡。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>挖掘者和建造者Tunnelers and Builders。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">狗頭人用掘穴和製作陷阱方面的天賦彌補了身體機能的缺陷。它們的巢穴設計成足以容納狗頭人輕鬆穿梭，而又能阻礙更大的類人生物通過的低矮地道。它們還在自己巢穴中佈滿陷阱。最隱蔽的狗頭人陷阱甚至會用上自然危害物和其他生物。一根絆繩也許連著一個倒出食肉綠軟泥的陶鍋，或是用張緊的彈簧陷阱向入侵者投擲帶毒的巨蜈蚣。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>失落的神靈The Lost God。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">除敬仰龍類外，狗頭人還崇拜一個名叫庫爾圖馬克Kurtulmak的弱等神。傳說庫爾圖馬克在侏儒之神加爾</span><span style=\"font-family:'MS Mincho'\">?</span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">閃金Garl Glittergold從龍後寶庫中偷走一件首飾之前曾是提亞馬特Tiamat在九獄的僕從。提亞馬特指派庫爾圖馬克取回首飾，但加爾</span><span style=\"font-family:'MS Mincho'\">?</span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">閃金卻使小伎倆破開土壤將庫爾圖馬克永遠困在了迷宮之中。因此，狗頭人們憎恨侏儒和任何惡作劇。庫爾圖馬克最虔誠的信徒們致力於尋找並將庫爾圖馬克從囚禁它的迷宮中釋放出來。<br /></span><span style=\"font-family:黑體\"><em><strong>帶翼狗頭人Winged Kobolds。</strong></em></span><span style=\"font-family:宋體\">少量狗頭人天生長着皮翼且可以飛行。這些被稱爲<em>厄德urds</em>的個體喜歡潛伏在高處的巖架上向路人投擲岩石。厄德的翅膀被視爲龍後提亞馬特的饋贈，同時也因此受無翼狗頭人的嫉妒而使得兩者無法融洽相處。</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(0, 0, 0);font-family:'Noto Sans SC';font-size:medium;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;margin:0pt\">Kobolds are craven reptilian humanoids that worship evil dragons as demigods and serve them as minions and toadies. Kobolds inhabit dragons' lairs when they can but more commonly infest dungeons, gathering treasures and trinkets to add to their own tiny hoards.</p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Strength in Numbers\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Strength in Numbers.</span> Kobolds are egg-laying creatures. They mature quickly and can live to be \"great wyrms\" more than a century old. However, many kobolds perish before they reach the end of their first decade. Physically weak, they are easy prey for predators. This vulnerability forces them to band together. Their superior numbers can win battles against powerful adversaries, but often with massive casualties on the kobold side.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Tunnelers and Builders\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Tunnelers and Builders.</span> Kobolds make up for their physical ineptitude with a cleverness for trap making and tunneling. Their lairs consist of low tunnels through which they move easily but which hinder larger humanoids. Kobolds also riddle their lairs with traps. The most insidious kobold traps make use of natural hazards and other creatures. A trip wire might connect to a spring-loaded trap that hurls clay pots of flesh-eating green slime or flings crates of venomous giant centipedes at intruders.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"The Lost God\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">The Lost God.</span> In addition to the dragons they revere, kobolds worship a lesser god named Kurtulmak. Legends speak of how Kurtulmak served as Tiamat's vassal in the Nine Hells until Garl Glittergold, the god of gnomes, stole a trinket from the Dragon Queen's hoard. Tiamat sent Kurtulmak to retrieve the trinket, but Garl Glittergold played a trick on him, collapsing the earth and trapping the kobold god in an underground maze for eternity. For this reason, kobolds hate gnomes and pranks of any kind. Kurtulmak's most devoted worshipers dedicate themselves to finding and releasing their lost god from his prison-maze.</p></div></div></div>",
        "public": ""
      },
